Aut is a humanoid with completely white skin. He has oversized hands and feet, but unnaturally gangly, thin arms and legs. His torso is a simple cylinder. His head is perfectly spherical, overly large, and has absolutely no facial features expect for a giant toothy grin that stretches from one side of his face to the other.

He makes a habit of observing the world, and nudging it in the direction he prefers through his "friends." The recent advent of the [[Voidsong]] has somehow disrupted his ability, however, much to his chagrin. He lives somewhere within the [[Geography/Black and White/index|Black and White]].

When Johnny Skyfall and Benny died at the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|Crowded Flea]], they met Aut in the empty space between [[Færrin]] and the [[Godhome]]. He told them that when people of Færrin die, their souls enter the [[Pharos]] and float up to the Godhome, and that this is the only way there. Because they had not come through the Pharos he would not let them into it from where they were, and instead pushed them back to the place they had died; each of them left a little of himself behind, whole but unable to grow, to be picked up later by returning through the Pharos. He set a mark on them, three blue dots in a triangle, which they can bring out or hide at will and which shows itself on its own to anyone who has already seen it. He said he can predict everything and cannot predict them, and blamed that on the Voidsong. He asked them to say hello to his friends at 13 Bright Street when they met them.

The Party met him again in the white void above Save Your Soul Incorporated, reached by the elevator's three-dot button. He called back the pieces of Johnny and Benny they had left in the Pharos, pushing two grey copies of them into their bodies, and both were whole again. He took questions and answered them.

He said the shades of the Black and White are native to it, and the dead of Færrin do not linger there. [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] was built around the site where Aurelia first climbed to the Godhome, and she used the Pharos; anyone who makes the trek to the Godhome and returns is a [[Hierophant|hierophant]], and a few are alive today, among them Aurelia VII. He said [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]] has to do with the [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]], and the Embercall is a derivative of the [[Voidsong]]. Of the [[Firmament|firmament]] he said it can be broken by destructive resonance: make the same sound inside and outside it and loud enough, and it gives way.

He said he had watched the Party only since they heard the Voidsong, and cannot predict those who have heard it, which is why [[Org/Amber Call/People/Benjamin Grayson|Master Grayson]] is a blank to him. He has friends in high places, more in [[Belvedere]] than in the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Church]], though the Pontifex herself does not approve of him; Cardinal Weatherhead is one of his, and Silas the guide is a Major-Chaplain. He gave up on the Inquisition, whose people tend to kill themselves after speaking with him.

He said Arctos is not the first speaking polar bear. There have been three: one was the pet of a sultan in [[Geography/Rhædon/index|Rhædon]] about 230 years ago, and one became sentient on its own in the Dark Ages and died at once. He marked Arctos at his request.

He told the Party that [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]] was at 412 Anchor Boulevard in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]], in the basement with four guards, one of them [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]], and predicted Hlarf's stop exactly: 27 hours on, shortly after four in the morning, Hlarf would park and get out drunk to piss in a fountain.

[[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs Marchal]] calls Aut the Writer, one of five siblings. He says they are not gods; they are the archetypal parts of a book. Aut designs the path he thinks a story should take, and his domain overlaps with his sister [[Divinity/The Narrative/Renge|Renge]], who is the things that might happen instead, so the two of them are at odds. Anaïs holds Aut responsible for the current prime minister, for the destruction of [[Geography/Raelion/index|Raelion]], for [[Geography/Brithwyn/index|Brithwyn]] breaking from [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]], for Aurthalaxus the Plaguebearer killing close to half of [[Færrin]]'s people some two hundred years ago, and possibly for the founding of [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] itself. He says Aut's foresight fails on anyone who has heard the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]], yet an ordinary person can still set a trap and catch such a listener by surprise.
